{
  "comment": "The words ME can hear. Each term's text vector is the mean of its prompts (the category templates with {} replaced by the term's text, or the term's own prompts), run through the pinned CLAP text encoder by build.ps1. Mood labels follow Plex's (AllMusic) mood names so they can stand in for missing Plex moods. Energy labels map to mix energy bands via 'band'. Aliases are extra words description search understands. 'calibration' is how strongly each category's terms are measured against the listener's library (0 = raw cosine, 1 = fully centred on the library's average for that term): text prompts carry their own bias toward music in general (raw, most songs 'sound' like Falsetto), while genre words line up with Plex tags best almost raw. 'scale' is the softmax sharpness. Both were tuned on 12,000 analysed songs; words CLAP confuses with commoner sounds (banjo with guitar, screaming with noisy synths) get prompts that carry their usual context. Groups marked \"describe\": false are for search only: Era can't be heard reliably enough to label a song (a modern song would always lean toward some decade), but it ranks songs well. Every word beyond the first 112 was kept only after it ranked a 39,000-song library well against that library's genre tags, release years or titles; words that didn't became aliases of their nearest honest stand-in or were left out (see README).",
